# Review ownership.
#
# CODEOWNERS on its own only requests reviewers. It does not require them —
# that needs branch protection with "Require review from Code Owners", which is
# a repository-admin setting and cannot be committed. Until an administrator
# enables it, everything below is advisory.
#
# The two paths that matter most:
#
#   corpus/verified/  is the published shared layer. An entry landing here is
#                     asserted to be true on a stated coordinate, and every
#                     consumer's default query returns it.
#   schemas/          is also the egress whitelist. additionalProperties:false
#                     is what stops an undeclared field leaving a fork, so
#                     widening any object here is a privacy decision.

